dh-uprising-time-up = Curfew: the Republic sends the army into the district. The uprising is over — for today.
dh-uprising-briefing-civilian = You are a resident of a Lost Angels district. The Military Police and the Front are fighting in your streets. Survive, work, and decide whom to trust.
dh-uprising-briefing-police = You are the Republican Military Police. LFFC cells are hiding among the residents: find and arrest or eliminate their squad leaders. Do not shoot civilians — every civilian killed counts against you.
dh-uprising-briefing-front =
    You are a fighter of the Liberation Front of Free Colonies.
    The Front was created in 2305 by the Independent Colonies out of prisoners, political convicts from execution lists, fugitives and those with nothing left to lose. The Front has no single ideology; it is held together by hatred of the old elites and of the Republic that built its capital on the slums of the lower levels. For thirteen years the Front's cells have smouldered in Lost Angels while the Military Police burned them out block by block. Your cell survived.
    Do not raise the uprising straight away. To everyone around you, you are an ordinary resident of the district: live, work, watch. Prepare the ground first. Learn where the MP patrols walk and where their posts stand, check the weapon caches, find sympathisers and those who would sell you out at the first chance. A fighter who shows himself too early dies for nothing and drags the whole cell down with him.
    Follow your squad leader; he will choose the moment to strike. The Independent Colonies armed you; your radio is on your ear. For liberty and justice for all!
dh-uprising-briefing-front-leader =
    You are a squad leader of the Liberation Front of Free Colonies.
    The Front was created in 2305 by the Independent Colonies out of prisoners, political convicts, fugitives and the desperate. Power in the Front rests on strength and fear, and right now that power is yours. For thirteen years the Front has waged a quiet urban war in Lost Angels. Today your cell can turn it into an uprising, if it does not rush.
    Do not raise the uprising straight away. Prepare the conditions first. Scout the Military Police patrols and posts, hand out the weapons from the caches, arrange communications, find sympathisers among the residents. Decide who in LA-V you can deal with: the corporation sells weapons to both sides. Move only when the cell is ready. An early move is a gift to the Military Police.
    Your goals: hold the district, strike the factory or broadcast the manifesto. Remember, the Front rests on you: if you are caught or killed, the uprising fails. The Independent Colonies armed you; your radio is on your ear. For liberty and justice for all!
dh-uprising-briefing-vanguard = You work for Lost Angels—Vanguard. The corporation sells to whoever pays. Protect the office and the representative.
dh-uprising-briefing-vanguard-vip = You are the LA-V representative in the district. Do business with both sides and get out alive: board the flight at LZ-1 Aeronautics (next in { $minutes } min).
dh-uprising-end-front = The district stays with the Front: { $free } of { $leaders } LFFC squad leaders remain free.
dh-uprising-end-police = The Military Police broke the uprising: every LFFC squad leader was arrested or killed.
dh-uprising-end-no-leaders = The uprising had no squad leaders.
dh-uprising-end-vip-evacuated = The LA-V representative got out through LZ-1 Aeronautics.
dh-uprising-end-vip-stayed = The LA-V representative did not get out.
dh-uprising-end-forces = Free and alive: Military Police { $police }, Front { $front }.
dh-uprising-end-civilians = Civilians killed: { $total } (by the Military Police: { $police }, by the Front: { $front }).
